From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shikosu <teovidal01@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 15:17:26 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] aot: svc reaches the Horizon service handler, thread
 pointers, services that map memory, cross-thread JIT invalidation (T5)

svc lifts (Remill patch 0003 kept in the fork) and calls aot_svc_handler with the shape of svc_dispatch, from AOT
code and from JIT code. tpidr_el0/tpidrro_el0 are per-run inputs. Guest regions can be added and removed while
guest threads run. A write by any thread invalidates every Jit that compiled from the page; a tight JIT loop is
sliced so that it sees the request. 14 tests against the Unicorn reference, including 8 concurrent host threads.

Upstream-Status: pending
Reason: svc, thread state and threading of the AArch64 -> x86_64 recompilation (NX2Linux); the host, loader and shader chain are untouched
Issue: none yet (NX2Linux, branch feat/teo-t5-svc-etat-invite)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
